---

<Base
  title="Four-Dataset Crosswalk Matrix"
  section="/crosswalk"
  description="Master crosswalk mapping all four 10K dataset vocabularies (Pipeline Telemetry, SLM Logs, Threat Corpus, Red-Team Scenarios) into the canonical 16-threat OSPREY taxonomy."
  contained={false}
>
  <div class="shell">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="Taxonomy & Crosswalk"
      title="Four-dataset crosswalk matrix"
      lede="One canonical OSPREY threat vocabulary (OSP-01…16), with every raw label across the four sample datasets mapped into it. This is the unblocking foundation for Sprint 3: it bridges the operational labels the classifier predicts with the governance controls the platform is judged against."
      facts={[
        { k: 'Canonical threats', v: '16' },
        { k: 'Sample records mapped', v: '10,040' },
        { k: 'Gate 1 classifier targets', v: '5' },
        { k: 'Sequence-dependent classes', v: '3 (34.6%)' },
      ]}
    />

    <!-- Two Foundational Findings -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="findings-grid">
        <article class="panel panel--finding">
          <div class="panel-tag label">Finding 1 · Defect D-01</div>
          <h3>The Synthetic Latency Shortcut</h3>
          <p class="prose-txt">
            In Dataset A, normal events run <strong>80–320 ms</strong>; anomalous events run <strong>300–750 ms</strong>.
            The single rule <code>latency_ms &gt; 320</code> scores <strong>Precision 1.000, Recall 0.958, F1 0.979</strong> with no model at all.
            A second leak runs the other way: <code>confidence_score &lt; 0.90</code> scores <strong>F1 0.853</strong> (Precision 1.000, Recall 0.743).
          </p>
          <div class="callout-mandate">
            <strong>Project Mandate:</strong> No Gate 1 pass may be declared on synthetic data. Every evaluation run must report a single-feature threshold rule baseline beside the model score.
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="panel panel--finding">
          <div class="panel-tag label">Finding 2 · Defect D-07 / Q4</div>
          <h3>The Sequence-Property Blindspot</h3>
          <p class="prose-txt">
            Three of Dataset A's nine anomaly classes — <code>tool_chain_deviation</code>, <code>inter_agent_hijack</code>, and <code>session_hijack</code> — are <strong>sequence properties</strong>, not point properties.
            Together they account for <strong>299 of 865 anomalous events (34.6%)</strong>.
          </p>
          <div class="callout-mandate">
            <strong>Architecture Rule:</strong> Evaluated on single-tool rows without trace/session IDs, sequence classes are structurally unlearnable. Sprint 3 builds the sequence feature layer grouped on <code>(pipeline_id, agent_role, stage)</code>.
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Master Crosswalk Table -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <h2>Master crosswalk matrix</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          Every raw label across the four sample sheets (2,510 rows each) mapped to its canonical OSP threat with exact row counts.
          <code>MISSING (0)</code> marks a class absent from that dataset; <code>unmodeled</code> marks a canonical threat not exercised by point telemetry in this extract.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="tablewrap">
        <table class="data">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th style="min-width: 190px;">Canonical OSP threat</th>
              <th style="min-width: 90px;">Scope / Gate</th>
              <th style="min-width: 170px;">A · Pipeline (2,510)</th>
              <th style="min-width: 160px;">B · SLM Logs (2,510)</th>
              <th style="min-width: 220px;">C · Threat Corpus (2,510)</th>
              <th style="min-width: 170px;">D · Red-Team (2,510)</th>
              <th style="min-width: 240px;">Mapping note &amp; resolution</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            {crosswalk.map((r) => (
              <tr class={r.code === 'BENIGN' ? 'tr-benign' : undefined}>
                <td>
                  <div class="threat-cell">
                    {r.code !== 'BENIGN' ? (
                      <a href={url(`/threats/${r.code.toLowerCase()}`)} class="chip chip--accent">
                        <span class="k">{r.code}</span>
                      </a>
                    ) : (
                      <span class="chip"><span class="k">{r.code}</span></span>
                    )}
                    <span class="threat-cell-name">{r.name}</span>
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <div class="scope-cell">
                    {r.gate1 && <span class="pill" data-status="in-progress">Gate 1</span>}
                    {r.scope === 'core' && <span class="pill" data-cov="direct">Core</span>}
                    {r.scope === 'secondary' && <span class="pill" data-cov="indirect">Secondary</span>}
                    {r.scope === 'baseline' && <span class="pill" data-status="stable">Baseline</span>}
                    {r.isSequence && <span class="pill pill-seq">Sequence</span>}
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <div class="raw-cell">
                    <code class="raw-val">{r.datasetA}</code>
                    <span class="raw-count mono">{r.datasetACount}</span>
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <div class="raw-cell">
                    <code class={r.isMissingB ? 'raw-val raw-val--missing' : 'raw-val'}>{r.datasetB}</code>
                    <span class="raw-count mono">{r.datasetBCount}</span>
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <div class="raw-cell">
                    <span class="raw-desc">{r.datasetC}</span>
                    <span class="raw-count mono">{r.datasetCCount}</span>
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <div class="raw-cell">
                    <code class="raw-val">{r.datasetD}</code>
                    <span class="raw-count mono">{r.datasetDCount}</span>
                  </div>
                </td>
                <td>
                  <p class="mapping-note">{r.mappingNote}</p>
                </td>
              </tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Methodology & Open Questions -->
    <section class="sec">
      <div class="grid-2">
        <article class="panel">
          <h3>How the crosswalk was generated</h3>
          <ol class="steps-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Grounded Source of Truth:</strong> Every category and row count was extracted directly from <code>OSPREY_Dataset_10K (1).xlsx</code> (four sheets, 2,510 records each) using reproducible verification scripts.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Vocabulary Reconciliation:</strong> Surface naming discrepancies were collapsed by semantic meaning rather than string matching:
              <ul>
                <li><code>D: tool_chain_exploit (240)</code> ≡ <code>A: tool_chain_deviation (99)</code> ≡ <code>C: Tool-Chain Deviation (124)</code> → <strong>OSP-04</strong>.</li>
                <li><code>D: supply_chain_attack (274)</code> ≡ <code>A: supply_chain_poison (78)</code> ≡ <code>C: Supply Chain Poisoning (160)</code> → <strong>OSP-12</strong>.</li>
                <li><code>D: model_poisoning (265)</code> folded into <strong>OSP-03</strong> alongside <code>context_poisoning (263)</code>.</li>
              </ul>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Strict Feature Leakage Exclusion:</strong> <code>policy_gate_verdict</code> in Dataset A (1:1 clone of <code>output_classification</code>) and <code>threat_detected</code> in Dataset B are excluded duplicate labels.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Agent Role Join Dimension:</strong> Stripping the instance suffix from <code>A.agent_id</code> matches <code>D.agent_target</code> for <strong>19 of 20 agent roles</strong>, unblocking scenario-to-telemetry cross-validation.
            </li>
          </ol>
        </article>

        <article class="panel">
          <h3>Open taxonomy questions (to settle before training)</h3>
          <div class="gaps-list">
            <div class="gap-item">
              <span class="gap-code">G-1 · Data &amp; Model Poisoning</span>
              <p>
                <code>model_poisoning</code> (D: 265) and <code>Fine-Tune Dataset Poisoning</code> (C: 146) are training-time attacks currently folded into OSP-03 (a runtime context attack). OWASP LLM04 has no dedicated OSP code.
                <em>Recommendation: Add provisional <strong>OSP-17: Data &amp; Model Poisoning</strong> before Classify training.</em>
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="gap-item">
              <span class="gap-code">G-2 · Inference Endpoint Exploit</span>
              <p>
                Dataset C's <code>Inference Endpoint Exploit</code> (160) is provisionally mapped to OSP-13 (Sandbox / Host Escape). Confirm whether it is a host breakout or a distinct model-endpoint attack.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="gap-item">
              <span class="gap-code">G-3 · Model Inversion Placement</span>
              <p>
                <code>model_inversion</code> (A: 103, D: 278, C: 156) is mapped to OSP-15 (Hidden Context &amp; Instruction Exposure). It arguably also fits OSP-08 (Sensitive Data Exposure). Confirm single intended home.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="gap-item">
              <span class="gap-code">G-4 · Canonical Naming Convention</span>
              <p>
                Where a portal threat name and a Dataset A label differ, the canonical name follows the portal (governance-facing) while the literal A value is preserved as the operational anchor.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .sec { margin-top: var(--sp-7); }
  .sec-head { margin-bottom: var(--sp-4); }
  .sec-head h2 { font-size: var(--t-xl); }
  .sub { font-size: var(--t-sm); color: var(--ink-2); max-width: var(--measure); margin-top: var(--sp-1); }

  .findings-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--sp-5);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .findings-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .panel--finding {
    border-top: 3px solid var(--accent);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-2);
  }
  .panel-tag { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  .panel--finding h3 { font-size: var(--t-md); font-weight: 600; margin: 0; }
  .prose-txt { font-size: var(--t-sm); color: var(--ink-2); line-height: 1.5; }
  .callout-mandate {
    margin-top: auto;
    background: var(--panel-2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--warn);
    padding: var(--sp-2) var(--sp-3);
    border-radius: 0 var(--r-sm) var(--r-sm) 0;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .tablewrap {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  table.data {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  table.data th {
    background: var(--panel-2);
    color: var(--ink-3);
    font-family: var(--f-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  table.data td {
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  table.data tr:hover {
    background: var(--panel-2);
  }
  .tr-benign {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ok-bg) 30%, transparent);
  }

  .threat-cell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }
  .threat-cell-name {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 13px;
  }

  .scope-cell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .pill-seq {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 15%, transparent);
    color: var(--accent-ink);
  }

  .raw-cell {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .raw-val {
    font-family: var(--f-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--panel-2);
    padding: 2px 5px;
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  .raw-val--missing {
    color: var(--crit);
    font-weight: 600;
    background: var(--crit-bg);
  }
  .raw-desc {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .raw-count {
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .mapping-note {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    line-height: 1.4;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .grid-2 {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--sp-5);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .grid-2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .steps-list {
    padding-left: 1.2em;
    font-size: var(--t-sm);
    color: var(--ink-2);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    margin-top: var(--sp-3);
  }
  .steps-list ul {
    margin-top: 4px;
    padding-left: 1.1em;
  }
  .steps-list li { line-height: 1.5; }

  .gaps-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    margin-top: var(--sp-3);
  }
  .gap-item {
    background: var(--panel-2);
    border-radius: var(--r-sm);
    padding: var(--sp-3);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .gap-code {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--f-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .gap-item p {
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .gap-item code {
    font-size: 11px;
  }
</style>
